WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Tesla's Robotaxi app now shows first rides free in Houston and Dallas as the service area expands nearly tenfold. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 650. Quiet mode on model y, robotaxis, overnight service hours, and the Tesla Semi's top gear award follow. Then first principles. Houston's Robotaxi promotion is not yet active in Austin, where cybercabs already operate, according to Drive Tesla Canada. The Houston Geofence grew from roughly 25 square miles to 250 miles.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:36.340
Tesla currently runs Robotaxi in seven markets, with fully autonomous rides in six of them.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.740
Earlier fairs included a flat $4.20 at launch, a later rise to $6.90, and then dynamic pricing

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.300
with a $1 base plus $1 per mile.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.580
CyberCab rides in Austin now run roughly 35% cheaper than Model Y Robotaxi's on the

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.100
same routes.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.140
The app labels eligible new users with first ride on us and a $0 fair.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:05.702
Tessla Extended Quiet Mode from the CyberCab to Model Y Robotaxies, Tessla Roddy Reports.

00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:10.862
Tapping a Crescent Moon icon strips out the map, the media player and app shortcuts,

00:01:11.462 --> 00:01:14.022
leaving only arrival details and essential controls.

00:01:14.702 --> 00:01:19.382
A Dallas Night Ride video showed the dark screen with arriving soon and a destination line.

00:01:20.022 --> 00:01:24.042
Turn signal chimes on Robotaxies now stop after the first four blinks.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:28.882
The feature first appeared on the CyberCab last week alongside a rear camera view,

00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:33.882
and Tesla has trimmed cabin noise without publishing formal release notes for either change.

00:01:34.402 --> 00:01:38.442
Elon Musk has talked about nap-friendly autonomous driving since 2014,

00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:43.522
raised the bar in 2017 to near-perfect reliability before riders would sleep,

00:01:44.022 --> 00:01:48.022
and in 2019 answered yes when owners asked for a similar nap mode.

00:01:48.895 --> 00:01:53.735
T.S. Oliming noted that robot taxi night hours from two to six in the morning stay closed,

00:01:54.095 --> 00:01:56.875
because the fleet has never driven that window driverlessly.

00:01:56.875 --> 00:02:00.595
That leaves no safety data for low-light hazards such as pets.

00:02:01.375 --> 00:02:06.195
Ashok said on the third quarter call that Tesla adds hours only after proving zero incident

00:02:06.195 --> 00:02:06.775
performance.

00:02:07.355 --> 00:02:09.655
He expects that gap to close by year-end.

00:02:10.195 --> 00:02:12.455
The cars can physically drive it three in the morning.

00:02:12.895 --> 00:02:16.575
The company still waits for enough driverless data before it opens the period.

00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:23.208
Top Gear gave the Tesla semi its 2027 tech award at the US car awards, according to

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:24.808
Reddit's Tesla Motors community.

00:02:24.808 --> 00:02:28.468
High volume output is increasing at the new Nevada factory.

00:02:28.788 --> 00:02:33.408
The award recognizes the truck's engineering at the moment that dedicated site is scaling

00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:33.928
volume.

00:02:34.861 --> 00:02:39.901
Pilot and FlyingJ truck stops now have Tesla semi-megachargers installed, according

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:40.821
to gadget review.

00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:45.861
Those stalls widen charging access for the growing semi-fleet on major freight corridors.

00:02:46.441 --> 00:02:52.141
The Berlin-built Model Y rear-wheel drive scored 93% overall in green and cap testing.

00:02:52.621 --> 00:02:54.061
Drive Tesla Canada reports.

00:02:54.061 --> 00:03:02.181
It received a perfect 10 out of 10 for greenhouse gas emissions and a life cycle footprint of 95 grams of CO2 equivalent per kilometer.

00:03:02.661 --> 00:03:13.921
It used 14.7 kilowatt hours per 100 kilometers in warm conditions and 21.3 on the highway and finished a 10 to 80% DC fast charge in 24 minutes.

00:03:13.921 --> 00:03:20.361
Green NCAP called that Model Y a benchmark for electric SUV efficiency, covering the German

00:03:20.361 --> 00:03:25.901
built version sold in Europe with verified data on raw materials, manufacturing, distribution

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.461
and lifetime operation.

00:03:28.101 --> 00:03:34.201
It also earned 8.9 out of 10 for energy efficiency and 9.0 out of 10 for clean air performance.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:39.721
Its heat pump and insulated cabin held heat even after 30 minutes powered down at minus

00:03:39.721 --> 00:03:40.861
7 degrees Celsius.

00:03:42.216 --> 00:03:45.436
CyberCab Robotaxies have started Interstate Rides in Austin.

00:03:45.856 --> 00:03:50.216
That step follows the initial public rollout of the purpose-built vehicle in the Texas

00:03:50.216 --> 00:03:50.756
Capitol.

00:03:51.476 --> 00:03:57.196
Tesla replaced its prior $250 vehicle referral credit with a new reward structure, according

00:03:57.196 --> 00:03:58.316
to electric vehicles.

00:03:58.816 --> 00:04:03.256
The referred driver gets a free month of full self-driving or FSD supervised.

00:04:03.736 --> 00:04:09.356
The referral gets either a free month or $99 in Tesla credits once the new user subscribes.

00:04:09.356 --> 00:04:12.196
The program launched only in the United States.

00:04:12.756 --> 00:04:17.296
Owners who refer someone receive the reward after the new subscriber activates the service.

00:04:17.896 --> 00:04:22.496
The change ties the incentive to full self-driving uptake rather than to vehicle purchases.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:31.690
Tesla Software 2026.38.5.1 breaks third-party vehicle-to-load adapters like Ella Joy according

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.330
to the Tesla Motors subreddit.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:38.330
Cars throw a battery discharge fault and end the session within 3-20 minutes depending

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:43.770
on load. Work around such as camp mode or service mode no longer keep the session running.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:49.210
Owners say the change arrives as Tesla expands its own power share vehicle to load offering.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:55.590
Those adapters previously worked on cars as old as a 2017 Model 3 with a CCS retrofit.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:01.070
One owner who had used an L-A-Joy unit daily for over a year and a half described turning off

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.650
the air conditioning, pausing music, opening the charge port, starting theater mode, and partly

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:12.320
closing the driver door before plugging in. Tesla urged Australia to put road user charges

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:17.780
on every vehicle rather than on electric cars alone, car expert reports. The position

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:23.771
comes as policy makers weigh distance-based fees that currently single out EVs. Tesla's

00:05:23.771 --> 00:05:28.071
shareholder letter asks investors to re-elect Elon Musk and two current board members.

00:05:28.591 --> 00:05:33.891
That request is in the material sent out ahead of the upcoming annual meeting. Indian diaspora

00:05:33.891 --> 00:05:38.671
buyers in the United States and Canada are the focus of a first-post piece on Tesla ownership.

00:05:39.211 --> 00:05:43.651
The article asks whether those cars read as a status symbol or as a practical purchase.

00:05:44.739 --> 00:05:50.359
Third-quarter profit at Tesla declined 43 percent, yet the stock rose afterward, according to

00:05:50.359 --> 00:05:55.619
mid-trade. The piece treats that reaction as a case study for Australian traders handling earnings.

00:05:56.239 --> 00:06:00.859
A veteran chip equipment executive said he had never seen this pace of execution at any prior

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:06.359
project, T.S. Alamming quoted after Elon Musk thanked contributors to the TerraFab effort.

00:06:06.919 --> 00:06:11.739
The remark points to progress on the AI training hardware well before the first wafer is produced.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:18.005
Photos show the next-gen Roadster parked under a Falcon 9 at SpaceX headquarters, next

00:06:18.005 --> 00:06:19.425
to the original design center.

00:06:19.905 --> 00:06:22.925
The car stood in the shadow of the rocket at the Hawthorne facility.

00:06:23.605 --> 00:06:27.405
Repeated rerouting and hesitation at intersections sat behind those times.

00:06:27.405 --> 00:06:32.205
The incidents show edge case handling still shaping the service as it grows beyond the

00:06:32.205 --> 00:06:33.165
first geofences.

00:06:33.745 --> 00:06:37.305
Tesla has not published updated release notes on that routing behavior.

00:06:37.825 --> 00:06:42.285
Similar reports have turned up in multiple markets where the fleet runs, with software

00:06:42.285 --> 00:06:45.645
confidence thresholds still deciding how reliable a trip feels.

00:06:46.655 --> 00:06:51.075
A three kilowatt load that once ran for hours is now the kind of session owners cannot

00:06:51.075 --> 00:06:53.075
count on from a third-party adapter.

00:06:53.075 --> 00:06:58.635
Forum members who track the change suspect Tesla now verifies that energy is actually flowing

00:06:58.635 --> 00:07:00.955
into the battery during any charging session.

00:07:01.395 --> 00:07:05.415
That would close a loophole that had lasted across multiple software generations.

00:07:06.075 --> 00:07:11.575
PowerShare itself was previously limited to Cybertruck and select Model Y trims, and Tesla

00:07:11.575 --> 00:07:13.835
branded hardware is still the narrower option.

00:07:14.615 --> 00:07:19.655
Owners who want a long discharge now face shorter sessions or a shift onto that official accessory

00:07:19.655 --> 00:07:19.955
path.

00:07:19.955 --> 00:07:24.775
The move concentrates value inside Tesla's own service and accessory channels.

00:07:25.175 --> 00:07:29.795
It also raises the switching costs for anyone who bought an older car expecting third-party

00:07:29.795 --> 00:07:30.835
gear to keep working.

00:07:31.535 --> 00:07:36.855
Every software controlled subsystem, from charging logic to cabin features, becomes a gate

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:38.855
that one update can tighten or open.

00:07:39.475 --> 00:07:43.535
A manufacturer that treats the vehicle as finished hardware lives under different constraints

00:07:43.535 --> 00:07:46.455
than one that can revise behavior fleet-wide overnight.

00:07:46.455 --> 00:07:49.535
Tesla gets faster iteration out of that model.

00:07:50.115 --> 00:07:54.955
Owners get a standing reminder that some future flexibility was traded for continuous improvement.

00:07:55.375 --> 00:08:00.555
That pattern feeds into residual value because a car that can gain capability or lose a work

00:08:00.555 --> 00:08:05.175
around years after purchase is a different asset than one whose hardware stays still.

00:08:05.855 --> 00:08:09.775
Tight vertical control over hardware and software lets the company move quickly.

00:08:10.355 --> 00:08:13.655
It also creates dependency on Tesla's own accessory roadmap.

00:08:13.655 --> 00:08:18.595
The honest tension is whether that continuous improvement helps owners more than a stable

00:08:18.595 --> 00:08:24.368
open platform would. Before we go, year end is the date Tesla has on opening those two

00:08:24.368 --> 00:08:29.068
to six morning robot taxi hours. And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

